/// A control that shows one of its items at a time, under a row of headers that the user taps, pans
/// or flicks through (WinUI's `Pivot`). The items are [`PivotItem`]s (other items get one as their
/// container). The pivot keeps one item selected while it has items
/// ([`SelectionMode::ALWAYS_SELECTED`]); setting
/// [`selected_index`](SelectingItemsControl::selected_index) flies the current item out and the new
/// one in, a pan of the content moves to the neighbour past a quarter of the width. With
/// [`is_header_items_carousel_enabled`](Self::is_header_items_carousel_enabled) (the default) the
/// headers and the items wrap around. [`is_locked`](Self::is_locked) keeps the selected item. The
/// structure is WinUI's (decision D8): the items are in a `ScrollViewer` (template part
/// `ScrollViewer`) whose content is a [`PivotPanel`] (`Panel`) a thousand sections wide, kept near
/// its middle by the pivot's state machine; the panel holds the `PivotLayoutElement` with the
/// headers and the `PivotItemPresenter`. During a pan the layout element stays in the viewport and
/// the items follow the content through expression animations of their `Translation`, on the
/// compositor (WinUI's secondary content relationships).
