/// The panel inside the scroll viewer of a [`Pivot`] (WinUI's `PivotPanel`): as wide as
/// [`PIVOT_PANEL_MULTIPLIER`] sections while the headers wrap, with a regular snap point at every
/// section, so that the scroll viewer pans one section at a time. Its child named
/// `PivotLayoutElement` (the headers and the items) is measured and arranged one section wide.
/// WinUI arranges it at the start of the panel and keeps it in the viewport with a secondary
/// content relationship of the scroll viewer; here it is arranged at the section the viewport rests
/// on (the pivot's section offset), and the pivot's composition expression keeps it in place during
/// a pan (a recorded deviation: layout and hit testing stay where the content is shown at rest).
